| 1 | `gcloud version` | Exit **0**; stdout includes a Google Cloud SDK / gcloud version ≥ **`minVersion`** |
| 2 | `gcloud help` | Exit **0** |

Run **`dryRuns`** with bare **`cli`** after install (Unix: after `~/bin`
symlinks exist). Full install-path executable is allowed only for an explicit
**`use-path`** override.

**Agent-shell `gcloud` (non-dry-run — binding):** When a lane runs **`gcloud`**
beyond dry-runs, follow **`rules/15_gcloud-multi-account.mdc`** — every command
includes **`--account=<gcloudAccountEmail>`** and project-scoped commands use
**`--project=<id>`**. **Forbidden:** **`gcloud config set account`**, **`gcloud config configurations activate`**, and relying on the global active account.

### `node`

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| **id** | `node` |
| **kind** | `cli` |
| **cli** | `node` |
| **minVersion** | `20.0.0` |
| **latestVersionProbe** | `curl -fsSL https://nodejs.org/dist/index.json` — select the **first** object whose **`lts`** is not **`false`**; parse **`version`** (e.g. `v22.14.0` → strip leading `v` for semver compare to installed `node --version`). **Windows zip artifact for install/upgrade:** `https://nodejs.org/dist/<version>/node-<version>-win-x64.zip` (keep the published `v` prefix inside `<version>`). **Forbidden:** probing or installing via Admin MSI as the upgrade channel. |
| **docsUrl** | https://nodejs.org/en/download/ |
| **installUrl** | https://nodejs.org/en/download/ |
| **macosInstallPath** | `~/.local/share/fnm/aliases/default/bin/node` |
| **linuxInstallPath** | `~/.local/share/fnm/aliases/default/bin/node` |
| **windowsInstallPath** | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\nodejs\node.exe` |

**macOS methods (`macosMethods`):**

| Method id | Notes |
|-----------|--------|
| `fnm-bootstrap` | **Sole** macOS method. **No Python.** Install [fnm](https://github.com/Schniz/fnm) when absent: `curl -fsSL https://fnm.vercel.app/install \| bash -s -- --install-dir "$HOME/.local/share/fnm" --skip-shell`. Ensure **`node`** and **`npx`** are on PATH for the agent shell (for example `eval "$(fnm env)"`). After consent: `fnm install 20` and `fnm default 20`. **Forbidden:** Homebrew as a substitute; **`pip`**; requiring Xcode CLT Python. |

**Linux methods (`linuxMethods`):**

| Method id | Notes |
|-----------|--------|
| `fnm-bootstrap` | **Sole** Linux method. Same fnm bootstrap and `fnm install 20` / `fnm default 20` as macOS. Ensure **`node`** and **`npx`** are on PATH (`eval "$(fnm env)"`). **Forbidden:** distro **`python3`** stacks for OOXML validation; ad-hoc **`pip`**. |

**Windows methods (`windowsMethods`):**

| Method id | Notes |
|-----------|--------|
| `fixed-path-zip` | **Sole** Windows method. Download the official Node.js **LTS** Windows **x64 binary zip** from nodejs.org via **`latestVersionProbe`** (URL pattern `https://nodejs.org/dist/<version>/node-<version>-win-x64.zip`). Extract so **`node.exe`** is exactly at **`windowsInstallPath`** (zip root layout is typically `node-<version>-win-x64\` containing `node.exe`, `npm.cmd`, `npx.cmd` — place those files in `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\nodejs\`; create directories as needed). Ensure that directory is on the **user** PATH so dry-runs can use bare **`node`** and **`npx`**. Prefer **`tar -xf`** or .NET `ZipFile` for extract. **Probe / PATH precedence:** follow the registry probe algorithm — **`use-path`** when supplied; else bare **`node`** / **`npx`** on PATH when they meet **`minVersion`** and dry-runs (existing Program Files MSI installs may qualify — do **not** force a zip reinstall); else incomplete LocalAppData install at **`windowsInstallPath`** routes to repair. When install/upgrade is required, write only to the LocalAppData **`windowsInstallPath`** tree (overwrite in place) — never Admin MSI / `%ProgramFiles%\nodejs\`. **Forbidden:** `nodejs-lts-msi` or any MSI/`msiexec` sole method; dual Windows sole methods; winget / Scoop / Chocolatey as sole method; open-ended install-directory questions; Electron-as-Node as inventory **`node`** (no bundled npm/`npx`); inventing Admin/UAC elevation as the recovery path. |

**dryRuns:**

| # | `command` | `expect` |
|---|-----------|----------|
| 1 | `node --version` | Exit **0**; stdout includes a semver ≥ **`minVersion`** |
| 2 | `npx --version` | Exit **0** |
| 3 | `bash .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-ooxml-validate.sh --self-test` | Exit **0**; resolves from hosting workspace center checkout |

Run dry-run **3** from the hosting workspace root when the center submodule is
present. On a center worktree pass, substitute the active **`CENTER_WORKTREE_ROOT`**
path: `bash "<CENTER_WORKTREE_ROOT>/scripts/docx-ooxml-validate.sh" --self-test`.

**Windows dry-run 3 (Git bash + `zip` — binding):** Dry-run **3** is a **bash**
script. On Windows, invoke it with **Git bash** (for example
`C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe`). The `--self-test` path builds a minimal
`.docx` with **`zip -qr`**, so a **`zip`** binary must be on **that bash PATH**.
Stock **Git for Windows** often ships **`unzip`** under `usr\bin` **without**
**`zip`** — dry-run 3 then fails with `zip: command not found` (**exit 127**)
even when Node/`npx` dry-runs 1–2 passed. **Keep this dry-run command unchanged** —
do not remove or rewrite row 3 to drop `zip`. Provide `zip` on the Git bash PATH
(install Info-ZIP/`zip`, or another package that puts `zip` where Git bash can
resolve it) before treating dry-run 3 as a Node install failure.

## Office binary (`.docx`) validation (binding)

Programmatic **writes** to **`.docx`** files (author / revision-author /
file-synchronizer lanes) must not rely on **`unzip -t`** or **`xmllint`**
alone — Word can reject packages that remain ZIP/XML-well-formed.

**Canonical validator:** center script
**`scripts/docx-ooxml-validate.sh`** (Node-first via **`npx`**
**`@xarsh/ooxml-validator@0.2.0`**, plus a hygiene gate rejecting prefixed
default xmlns on **`[Content_Types].xml`** and **`*.rels`**).

| Phase | Agent obligation |
|-------|------------------|
| **Prerequisite** | **`node`** and **`npx`** on PATH — probe/install via **`node`** in **Tool inventory** and mission **`install required tools`**. On Windows, **Git bash** plus **`zip`** on that bash PATH are also required for **`--self-test`** / dry-run 3 (see **Windows dry-run 3** under tool **`node`**). **Forbidden:** Python OOXML stacks on end-user workstations. |
| **Before outbound sync** | Run **`docx-ooxml-validate.sh`** on the absolute **`.docx`** path. **Fail closed** on non-zero exit — do not **`bisync`** / **`sync`**. |
| **After material edit** | Same validation gate before any outbound push when the lane edited the **`.docx`** in-process. |

**Invoke (from hosting workspace or center worktree):**

```bash
bash .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-ooxml-validate.sh "/absolute/path/to/file.docx"
```

Substitute **`CENTER_WORKTREE_ROOT/scripts/docx-ooxml-validate.sh`** when editing
under an active center worktree.

## Pending OOXML markup script (binding)

**Canonical markup helper:** center script **`scripts/docx-markup.mjs`** (Node-only).
**Forbidden:** Python OOXML stacks for pending markup.

| Subcommand | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| **`mark-insert`** | Wrap new text in `w:ins` with `w:author` / `w:date` |
| **`mark-delete`** | Wrap removed text in `w:del` |
| **`mark-red`** | Apply `w:color FF0000` to the run containing `--text` |
| **`list-pending`** | JSON report: `insCount`, `delCount`, `redRunCount`, `pending` |
| **`accept-all`** | Flatten track changes; strip red color |

**Invoke (from hosting workspace or center worktree):**

```bash
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-markup.mjs list-pending "/absolute/path/to/file.docx"
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-markup.mjs mark-insert "/absolute/path/to/file.docx" --text "new prose"
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-markup.mjs mark-delete "/absolute/path/to/file.docx" --text "text to remove"
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-markup.mjs mark-red "/absolute/path/to/file.docx" --text "text to highlight"
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-markup.mjs accept-all "/absolute/path/to/file.docx"
```

Substitute **`CENTER_WORKTREE_ROOT/scripts/docx-markup.mjs`** when editing under an
active center worktree. Default **`w:author`**: **`Sedea Author Agent`** (`--author`
override optional). After every markup mutation, run **`docx-ooxml-validate.sh`**
(fail closed). **`list-pending`** and **`accept-all`** are the **binding interface**
for author / sync / reviewer skills — do not substitute ad-hoc XML for those operations.

## Outbound sync pending-markup gate (binding)

**Canonical gate helper:** center script **`scripts/docx-outbound-sync-gate.mjs`**
(Node-only). Applies to **outbound** **`rclone bisync`** / **`sync`** paths only
(inbound §4 pull is **not** gated by pending markup).

| Input | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| **`--markup-pending true`** | **Block** sync (exit 1) — trust upstream author skill output |
| **`--markup-pending false`** | **Allow** sync (exit 0) — pending cleared per upstream lane |
| **Omitted** | Run **`list-pending`** on the absolute **`.docx`** path; block when `pending: true` |

**Invoke (from hosting workspace or center worktree):**

```bash
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-outbound-sync-gate.mjs \
  --markup-pending true "/absolute/path/to/file.docx"
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-outbound-sync-gate.mjs \
  "/absolute/path/to/file.docx"
node .sedea/centers/documentation-management/scripts/docx-outbound-sync-gate.mjs --self-test
```

Substitute **`CENTER_WORKTREE_ROOT/scripts/docx-outbound-sync-gate.mjs`** when editing
under an active center worktree. **Fail closed** on exit **1** — do not run outbound
**`bisync`** / **`sync`**. Binding surfaces: Author Simple Document §7, Author
Multi-Part §9, and **`file-synchronizer`** outbound **`rclone sync`**.

Mitigation context: doc authoring track-changes PRD (dispatch `f6020f03-9121-413c-b6e4-d1e881fae704`).

## Document extraction during gathers (binding)

During **gather** steps that read user-supplied documents (SoT **`documents`**
intake and similar flows), agents must prefer **OS-native and already-present**
extractors before any package install. This section defines **default extract
paths** — it does **not** add rows to **Tool inventory** below (those tools use
the install registry; extractors here are OS-builtin).

### macOS default: PDF text extract

On **macOS** (`uname -s` = `Darwin`), the **default** PDF **text extract**
path is **JXA + PDFKit** via **`osascript -l JavaScript`** — not `textutil`,
not ad-hoc **`pip install pypdf`**, not assumed **`pdftotext`**.

| Priority | Method | When |
|----------|--------|------|
| 1 | Center script **`scripts/pdf-extract.jxa`** | Preferred — canonical wrapper; args: absolute PDF path, optional max page cap |
| 2 | Inline JXA + PDFKit | Same semantics when the script path is unavailable |
| 3 | `pdftotext` on PATH | Only after JXA returns empty **and** the user approves fallback at a gather USER_CHECKPOINT |
| — | `textutil -convert txt` on `.pdf` | **Forbidden** — emits raw PDF bytes, not text |
| — | `pip` / `brew` for PDF Python stacks | **Forbidden** on gather unless this section or an explicit developer request names the tool |

**Vanilla Mac obligation:** On hosts **without** Homebrew, poppler, or Xcode
CLT, JXA + PDFKit remains available via `/usr/bin/osascript` and
PDFKit.framework — do not treat missing `pdftotext` as grounds for
`pip install`.

**Large / scanned PDFs:** Cap pages (script optional arg or inline
`Math.min(n, cap)`). Empty extract on image-only PDFs → report at
USER_CHECKPOINT; do not auto-`pip`.

**Stub CLIs (binding):** Do **not** invoke `/usr/bin/python3` or
`/usr/bin/swift` on hosts where they are Xcode CLT install stubs (install
dialog / hang).

### Other formats (macOS probe order)

| Format | Default extract |
|--------|-----------------|
| `.txt`, `.md`, `.csv` | Read directly |
| `.rtf`, `.html`, `.doc`, `.docx`, `.odt` | `textutil -convert txt -stdout FILE` (**read/gather only** — not a write-validation gate) |
| `.xlsx` / `.pptx` | `unzip -p` on OOXML parts (lossy) — prefer registry tools if later added |
| Images | `file`, `sips`, `qlmanage -t` (metadata/thumbnail — not document text) |

**Programmatic `.docx` edits** (Write / StrReplace / OOXML rewrites on the working
file) are **not** gather reads — apply **Office binary (`.docx`) validation**
above before outbound sync. **`textutil`** and lossy unzip probes do **not**
substitute for **`docx-ooxml-validate.sh`**.

### Package install boundary

1. **Tool inventory** below is the **sole** install surface for **`rclone`**,
   **`gcloud`**, Sedea extensions, etc. — route gaps via mission
   **`install required tools`** (**detached dispatch**).
2. **`pip` / `brew` / ad-hoc installs** during gather are **forbidden** unless
   **this section** or an **explicit developer request** names the tool —
   state why before any install attempt.
3. Do **not** add **`pypdf`**, **`python-docx`**, or **`openpyxl`** to gather
   flows by default.

Mitigation for premature pip during SoT gather:
[documentation-management#60](https://github.com/sedea-centers/documentation-management/issues/60).

## Agent obligations

1. Treat this inventory as the **only** required-tools source for this center.
2. Branch by **`kind`**. For `sedea-extension`, use the Sedea CLI probe/install
   contract above; never use another editor's extension profile. For `cli`,
   probe in order: (a) any **user-supplied path/command** from the install mission
   gate; (b) `command -v` / PATH on **`cli`**; (c) if PATH misses, check the
   resolved OS install path for incomplete-install detection only. Do not invent
   alternate install directories. Do not PATH-prepend SDK `bin/` as normal policy.
3. Compare discovered binary or extension version to **`minVersion`** — classify
   **missing**, **outdated** (below `minVersion`), or candidate **ok**. When
   candidate **ok** and **`latestVersionProbe`** is defined, run it — latest &gt;
   installed → **upgrade-available**; otherwise **ok**. Incomplete CLI resolution
   counts as **missing**.
4. Install or **upgrade** only after structured-choice consent (**install** or
   **upgrade**, not method/path choice). Use the **sole** listed OS method id.
   For `cli`, place the binary exactly at the OS install path and follow method
   notes and **`installUrl`** (including Unix **`gcloud`** `~/bin` symlinks). For
   `sedea-extension`, install/upgrade through the resolved Sedea CLI per method
   notes (gallery id **or** pinned VSIX download + path) with `--force` without
   bundling. **Forbidden:** method pickers; install-directory questions;
   inventing latest-version sources not listed as **`latestVersionProbe`**.
5. After install, upgrade, or path override, run **every** **`dryRuns`** row in order
   with bare **`cli`** for `cli` tools or the resolved Sedea CLI for
   `sedea-extension` tools, then record pass/fail.
6. For Drive **`lsf`** / **bisync**, apply **Drive auth invoke** — SA flags and
   probe order — before suggesting **`rclone config reconnect`**.

